# styles.css `!important` policy

In `src/styles/styles.css`, **only** the `[hidden]` polyfill may use `!important`:

```css
[hidden] {
  display: none !important;
}
```

That polyfill is required because browsers no longer give `[hidden]` UA-level `!important`, and author `display:` rules must not defeat it.

## Do

- Prefer higher specificity or later cascade order instead of `!important`.
- Keep view/theme/`[hidden]` conflicts solvable without new `!important`s.
- Leave the existing `[hidden]` polyfill `biome-ignore` alone (Biome needs it for that one exception).

## Do not

- Add new `!important` in `styles.css`.
- Add `biome-ignore lint/complexity/noImportantStyles` to waive new `!important`s — Biome ignores do **not** satisfy the unit-test invariant in `test/unit/editor-wrap-cascade.test.js` (“only [hidden] polyfill may use !important”).
- Assume print.css / injected preview CSS policies apply to `styles.css`; this rule is specific to the main stylesheet.

`npm test` / pre-commit (`npm run precommit`) will fail if `styles.css` gains extra `!important` declarations.
